---
import HeldDemo from './HeldDemo.svelte';
---

<section id="held" class="drench on-honey py-(--space-section)" aria-labelledby="held-title">
  <div class="wrap grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="label section-index text-ink-soft">04 / Held deliveries</p>
      <h2 id="held-title" class="headline mt-6">Switch it off. Nothing is lost.</h2>
      <p class="lead mt-8">
        A switched-off deployment holds its deliveries instead of dropping them. Held runs cost nothing,
        never time out and never start by accident.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-[46ch] text-ink-soft">
        Turning it back on does not replay a week of work. Releasing the backlog is a decision you make, and
        each delivery runs as it arrived: same payload, oldest first.
      </p>
      <p class="label mt-10 inline-block rounded-sm bg-ink px-3 py-2 text-honey">
        Try it: switch off, wait, switch on, release
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:pt-4">
      <HeldDemo client:visible />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
